    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d543">

                <pb facs="0608" n="596" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg596"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/16685</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-11-10">November 10, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The French Ambassador called on the President at the former’s request and I was
                    present on the invitation of President Roosevelt. The Ambassador complained
                    again about the British action at Djibouti. He, of course, understands the
                    grounds on which the British action was based, but he was careful not to mention
                    that phase of the matter. Very little was said in reply to him in this
                    regard.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
